\ stages/s6-genes.4 - s6-cv8b's genes for forth/cross-cv8.4, written by lab/evolve/export-genes.py from the
\ options the evolver hands the translator (tools/layout.py) and the engine's flags. Include it before
\ cross-cv8.4: S" extend.4" INCLUDED  S" genes.4" INCLUDED  S" cross-cv8.4" INCLUDED
\ A list is a word giving its text ( --- c-addr u ), names and numbers each followed by one space.
VARIABLE G-AT
: G-LIST: ( "name" --- ) CREATE HERE G-AT ! 0 , DOES> DUP CELL+ SWAP @ ;
: G+ ( c-addr u --- ) DUP G-AT @ +! HERE SWAP DUP ALLOT CMOVE ;
: G-C ( c --- ) HERE C! 1 ALLOT 1 G-AT @ +! ;
8 CONSTANT G-CELL          \ the target's cell, bytes
G-LIST: G-OVERLAYS  \ after kernel.4, in this order
S" cv8.4 cv8b.4 " G+
G-LIST: G-FOLDS  \ the fold set: FOLD-BASE + place
S" + = ! @ LSHIFT RSHIFT C@ C! AND OR XOR LIT < U< OVER DROP DUP SWAP ROT >R R> R@ NEGATE " G+
31 CONSTANT G-SPEC          \ the specialisations: 1 small, 2 imm, 4 var, 8 tiny, 16 loc
G-LIST: G-SUPERS  \ fused pairs: first second opcode
G-LIST: G-OPS10  \ format-10 operations: name opcode
0 CONSTANT G-HOTCALLS      \ one-byte calls, at most
0 CONSTANT G-OP-BODIES     \ the format-10 words' bodies their opcode
0 CONSTANT G-OP-INLINE     \ ...placed among the primitives
0 CONSTANT G-BSS           \ TIB, POCKET, INCLUDE-BUFFER past the image's end
0 CONSTANT G-THIN-HEADER   \ one empty thread head in the file
32 CONSTANT G-THREADS       \ the dictionary's hash threads
0 CONSTANT G-HASHK         \ the chain hash's K (hashk; 0: kernel.4's hash)
0 CONSTANT G-RTFUSE        \ the run-time fuser's tables filled (cv8-fuse.4's SUPER-TABLE, IMM-OPS)
0 CONSTANT G-ESCAPE         \ escaped primitives: two bytes, ESC and a selector
G-LIST: G-ESC-PRIMS  \ the escaped primitives
-1 CONSTANT G-VARSLOT        \ slot operands 2 or 3 bytes, high byte first; else 2, low first
G-LIST: G-REBIND  \ the kernel's uses rebound to the overlays' words
G-LIST: G-HEADERLESS  \ no headers
G-LIST: G-SKIP  \ definitions the translator drops
0 CONSTANT G-CHAINORDER    \ each chain its most looked-up names first (layout.py --chainorder; 732, 736)
G-LIST: G-CO-HOT  \ ...those names, and how often the held-out programs look each up
G-LIST: G-TRIM8  \ an overlay's NAME8 that is NAME
G-LIST: G-ONCE  \ names only their first definition makes
1 CONSTANT G-ENGINE-SPEC   \ the engine's flags: SPEC (the locals block in the header)
31 CONSTANT G-FEATURES      \ the image's feature bits (engine/vm-lab.c's IMAGE_MAGIC)
76 CONSTANT G-MAGIC5
0 CONSTANT G-TAG2          \ the two-bit tag: codes by the engine's map, calls 2-4 bytes, links 1-4
0 CONSTANT G-T2WIDE        \ ...no 3-byte call: 0x80-0xBF one-byte codes
G-LIST: G-T2-ONE  \ the engine's map: logical operation, one-byte code
G-LIST: G-T2-ESC  \ ...logical operation, escape selector
0 CONSTANT G-JIT           \ the lazy JIT (engine/jit.c): its opcode a tag-2 code
0 CONSTANT G-JITIMG        \ 1: the outer interpreter's words given the JIT header
0 CONSTANT G-JITDEAD       \ the gene jitdead: the JIT header the code alone, bodies four bytes (723)
0 CONSTANT G-JITX          \ --jitx: every code word in jit_wends
0 CONSTANT G-GUARD-ABORT   \ the gene abortif: ABORT" guarded by ?BRANCH (sod16.guard_aborts; 714)
G-LIST: G-HOT-INLINE  \ calls inlined: caller callee k (the k-th call), as the translator chose them
0 CONSTANT G-FACTOR        \ the gene factor: repeated cold code in headerless bodies (layout.py --factor; 715)
0 CONSTANT G-FACTOR-ANY    \ ...every word, the profile aside (--factor-share above 1)
G-LIST: G-FACTOR-COLD  \ ...the words below --factor-share of the reference dispatches
G-LIST: G-FACTOR-NOT  \ ...never: what layout.py patches after reading it, the dump tool
G-LIST: G-NOT-YET  \ the translator's options the cross compiler does not do yet
